#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189179} :activity/id #uuid "831069d2-736b-52d1-a2bb-6631187686b5" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049908 :topic/id #uuid "1dc40382-49d1-5d5b-a59d-1be47c4f903d" :topic/math-academy-id 3929} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189179 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189404 :tutorial/content "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are continuous random variables, where the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is given by $\\mu_{X|y}.$ In other words,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] = \\mu_{X|y}.\n$$\n\nThe **conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$** is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y] = \\textrm{E}\\big[(X - \\mu_{X|y} \\big)^2 \\,|\\, Y=y].\n$$\n\nAs with the discrete case, this definition can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}\\big[X^2 \\,| \\, Y=y \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} x^2 \\, f_{X|Y}(x \\,|\\, y) \\: \\textrm{d}x,\n$$\n\n \n\nand $f_{X|Y}(x \\,|\\, y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ Note that these formulas are analogous to those for $\\textrm{Var}[X]$ for continuous $X.$\n\nWhen we select a particular value of $y,$ the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ returns a real number. However, if $y$ is not specified, then $\\textrm {Var}[X | Y = y]$ gives us a *function* of $y.$\n\nWe have an analogous definition for the **conditional variance of $Y$ given  $X=x{:}$**\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n- $\\mu_{Y|x} = \\textrm{E}\\big[Y \\,| \\, X=x \\big]$ is the conditional expected value of $Y$ given  $X=x,$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\textrm{E}\\big[Y^2 \\,| \\, X=x \\big] = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} y^2 \\, f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, x) \\: \\textrm{d}y,$ and\n\n- $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ is the conditional probability density function of $Y$ given $X=x.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "cc60678b-fd8c-537f-99be-cee66503c859" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6444 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "90a5c594-6537-5336-90c2-6eca3c31d58b" :step/math-academy-id 38946 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189203}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189180 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188336 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188043 :question/id #uuid "ea6a79c4-09fc-5ae9-9e92-e7bacd4939d9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10340"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29e185b1-7bd3-5441-b502-3049a253cf3e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049871} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050965}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188655} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188721} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530440} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530445} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530459} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530488} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530502}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF"} :step/id #uuid "53d73871-be25-53a5-8455-4cf04e078787" :step/math-academy-id 38947 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189181}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189181 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188337 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188044 :question/id #uuid "fef21fcb-bab6-5f33-a792-280e28a97f81" :question/math-academy-id "e-10341"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aadf2ac8-bfb4-5371-97c3-1ae194c9479f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188722} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188724} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530417} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530464} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530494} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530508} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545864}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional PDF Using Improper Integrals"} :step/id #uuid "7bbe5d6f-436a-56b7-b6c3-4b50cf86ea46" :step/math-academy-id 38948 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189182}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189182 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188338 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188045 :question/id #uuid "acb4923c-ce04-5cd5-af01-2f078a18ceed" :question/math-academy-id "e-10342"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fa6c30c5-e8c2-502d-abac-5d54f0b6f2fc" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188661} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188719} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530439} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530444} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530448} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530535} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186530546} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545860} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545877}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given Joint and Marginal Density Functions"} :step/id #uuid "e3ab0323-0d1c-5360-8b97-deeb42c28a59" :step/math-academy-id 38949} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189203 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189410 :tutorial/content "Suppose that ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) and ![](images/ab/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) are continuous random variables. It is known that the conditional probability density function ![](images/93/939d0476e164e1f946f2c1f56829e1d23d0f14cf794d59ed194139e9ca0c6633.svg) is given by\n\n![](images/01/01cc971ff9be09d98f7b82c17dcb437308e0db1bb748bfad31f76a1f5be54828.svg)\nand that\n![](images/26/267e370c58b7350ddf932adcbe95f9b51a895c4d970f2d5ed8313bfd050a215c.svg)\nWhat is the conditional variance ![](images/fc/fc8d9d3eba8e082c14369171fd86c8786ec9efbb70b3d6a840f4cec11740be79.svg)\n\nThe conditional variance of ![](images/ab/ab4817775494786b06f0b9cecf225ea5979c035b69c36c1fa078f835524be9e9.svg) given ![](images/2c/2cc57b1c8b00862c078193ea1774f4012e1513ab1a26a6d5bb806e046220a812.svg) is defined by\n\n![](images/82/82fb648d48cfe25c760b67838480f3b464ae25f5107a13fbecea46b1d47f543c.svg)\n\nwhere \n\n![](images/b1/b1ba1db07783ff23a06aff81a65993cc776777cdb471c20074d3ceac8db820a1.svg)\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n![](images/da/daf6a9ae8a295a2120e9720260b9c62d984774107bc2fc2308d60f027ac5f0d4.svg)\n\nFinally,\n\n![](images/97/97c0423f3c9f02779731969b447d9fa6040eb7637e541d7cdcdb9e68037477d7.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "51fd1dbf-d36f-5e8c-b62b-ede292dae6da" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6490 :tutorial/title "A Worked Example"} :step/id #uuid "0112f403-404f-5282-8492-4ad12782a53c" :step/math-academy-id 39321 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189180}}] :activity/title "Conditional Variance for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186188512}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545964} :activity/id #uuid "df6d61a7-cd86-5ac5-97fc-01ff756a34b2" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049908 :topic/id #uuid "1dc40382-49d1-5d5b-a59d-1be47c4f903d" :topic/math-academy-id 3929} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545887 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3da82ce9-78a2-543b-b42d-6a1dff04ede5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{200}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545317} {:answer/id #uuid "73f2b6d9-290a-5c57-9e0d-31e098d34378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545418} {:answer/id #uuid "840b7aa1-f717-5655-85ec-596b4ab1d025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{200}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545448} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7dd604-9a13-5ed1-a0b7-6e46c2373cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545575} {:answer/id #uuid "f1e99de4-ede4-589b-af99-ad16705b718a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545646}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545448} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a1b473-68e4-5c3b-8125-45d0cb822b91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cb67f6a8-9365-5c2f-8040-e07ca796601e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146390" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{7}xy, & 0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{7}y(4-{y}^{2}), & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|\\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{7}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{8}{7}xy}{\\frac{4}{7}y(4-{y}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{4-{y}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le 2.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{2x}{(4-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2})}=\\frac{2x}{(\\frac{15}{4})}=\\frac{8}{15}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{15}x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}{\\int }_{1/2}^{2}{x}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{1/2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}[{x}^{4}]_{1/2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}(16-\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\cdot \\frac{255}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}]-{\\mu }_{X|\\frac{1}{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{8}-{(\\frac{7}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{8}-\\frac{49}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{200}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0d528e79-53bc-5be0-992d-62a18f4c262f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545910}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545904 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545864 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3704891e-617a-5863-9a03-baf25c99600b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545312} {:answer/id #uuid "3a4c20c4-9a93-56b4-8882-ad1c931d6d09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545315} {:answer/id #uuid "77363dd6-1e0e-5193-8140-a9949d0605e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545421} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d98834-f4f5-587e-83de-a18d83a26a86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{36}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545615} {:answer/id #uuid "eed61002-51ff-5a1c-9ad4-f4d067a9f8d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545644}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545615} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d2588d2-34f5-552a-8d6d-c5e7c03f7737" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da13a004-2a50-58d1-9227-22e3b27eef81" :question/math-academy-id "q-149429" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3{y}^{11/3}}, & \\,1\\le y \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=4]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|4}=\\frac{8}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=4] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3{y}^{11/3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{3{y}^{5/3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{3}{y}^{-5/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{8}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot {y}^{-2/3}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{4}{{y}^{2/3}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =0-(-4) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=4] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=4]-{\\mu }_{Y|4}^{2} \\\\  & =4-{(\\frac{8}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{64}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "30b66353-4193-5326-899b-b7131edd7f72"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545910 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af426a61-873a-54e8-87e7-c5268f358e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186613} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a125c4-79a7-5fc7-8d69-81df40d1a785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186614} {:answer/id #uuid "104fbeb9-321b-5cf2-a901-4e2171ef33e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186615} {:answer/id #uuid "291d2635-4024-5090-9a86-02fd630f782c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186616} {:answer/id #uuid "59ac25e1-139f-55c2-acdd-07c0ae67efdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186617}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186186615} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ff21e41-edd8-56fc-b9a8-ac593324b506" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186612}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ab2b344e-989b-53e3-aa40-0cb9cb3e7391" :question/math-academy-id "q-146773" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2{y}^{7/2}}, & \\,1\\le y \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|3}=\\frac{5}{3}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=3] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2{y}^{7/2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5}{2{y}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-5\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}]}_{1}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=3]-{\\mu }_{Y|3}^{2} \\\\  & =5-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{25}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3b11e1b9-606d-568a-aff8-39bd701af3dd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545919}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545919 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "155ff5aa-4252-5ac2-80e1-ab36e6819d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{37}{450}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545238} {:answer/id #uuid "63386fd4-c351-5fcf-a204-868e364ac71f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{350}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545386} {:answer/id #uuid "9519ed18-f682-5e18-95a3-d2bb7a09c5cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{45}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545469} {:answer/id #uuid "bd742401-7fbe-51ac-b99e-fa8961304350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{19}{225}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545544} {:answer/id #uuid "efcb4a86-108b-540b-8958-93dcf800b027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{450}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545238} :answer-field/id #uuid "08777c93-71f1-55d9-8b74-18999d083645" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fa5bb889-1d66-5ec8-b499-bab2b60bc9f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-146830" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+4y}{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{8}{15}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3})}{(\\frac{1+4y}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+2y)}{1+4y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$ \n\nNow, substituting $y=1$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\frac{2(x+2\\cdot 1)}{1+4\\cdot 1}=\\frac{2x+4}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(\\frac{2x+4}{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{4}{3})-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\frac{11}{6}] \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=1]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{30}-{(\\frac{8}{15})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{37}{450}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4a39c991-2450-5455-97eb-6d1a8a8ba947" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545904}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545964 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188661 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aac95833-5753-59ed-9064-3dce9eb6bf55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186247} {:answer/id #uuid "10e80e17-c1da-540f-920f-b561444e71ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{23}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186248} {:answer/id #uuid "391b2f77-21a7-5d46-a4db-4f999030277f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186249} {:answer/id #uuid "72246038-c9c6-578f-bb17-dada1cfec565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186250} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9b3625-cb76-501b-acae-fb328a041f55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{144}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186251}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186186250} :answer-field/id #uuid "a645beee-fbf3-56f4-b659-c712fa82e7d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cc5459e2-e87e-5998-9738-d0d2044cb502" :question/math-academy-id "q-145870" :question/problem "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}+y, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|\\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{7}{12}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ is a function of $y.$ \n\nThe conditional density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ can be computed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+y}{\\frac{1}{2}+y} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+y)}{1+2y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$ Outside this domain, we have ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=0.$\n\nNow, substituting $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the expression for ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{2(x+\\frac{1}{2})}{1+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{2x+1}{2}=x+\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}] & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}(x+\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{6})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}]-{\\mu }_{X|\\frac{1}{2}}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-{(\\frac{7}{12})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-\\frac{49}{144} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{144}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "aad3c882-96ee-5b93-a8e5-1fd98a1acdf4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545887}}] :activity/title "Conditional Variance for Continuous Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545197}]}
